  "_about": "Source list for illustrations/*.svg, built by scripts/prep_illustration.py. 'src' is a Wikimedia Commons file title; licence and author are read from Commons, never typed here ('author' overrides only the NAME when Commons' artist line is long or wrong). 'key' labels become bold (the labelling card's pins, in this order); 'translate' rewrites label text; 'drop' removes labels whose text matches; 'keep' keeps only these labels; 'leave' marks text that is part of the drawing (not re-set); 'join' names labels written as one text per line ('Small' over 'intestine'); 'nudge' {label: [dx, dy]} moves a label; 'hide' [CSS selectors] removes parts of the file (a dropped label's leader line); 'page': true keeps only what lies on the file's own canvas, clipped to it; 'add' [{text, x, y, anchor, to:[x, y]}] places a label OURSELVES in the file's viewBox units, with a leader line to 'to' - a claim about the drawing, so name parts only from the author's own labelled version or legend, and look. 'title' is what the learner sees. '_note' is for people.",
